From: Flax Advisors
Subject: firmware: hide "Backup image" cards on the Firmware page

The Firmware page renders a "Backup image" card alongside the running
image for both BMC and Host (BIOS) firmware.  These cards are driven
by upstream's dual-image / A-B-slot model (firmware inventory id
"bmc_bkup" and the Host equivalent).

The TiogaPass build uses phosphor-software-manager with
bmc-static-dual-image=disabled and a single-image flash layout, so no
"bmc_bkup" entry ever appears in
/redfish/v1/UpdateService/FirmwareInventory and the Backup card
permanently shows "--".  The empty card and its inert "Switch to
running" button look like a feature an administrator can use and lead
to support questions.

Remove the Backup card from both BMC and Host card groups.  The
Running card (BMC and Host) and the Host "Clear configuration" toggle
are unchanged.  The IconSwitch import in FirmwareCardsBmc.vue was
used only by the now-removed "Switch to running" button; drop it so
the build passes eslint's no-unused-components rule.  The modal and
switch-to-running action method are left in place to keep this patch
surgical.

